# health-guard-beacon.json was checked and correctly excluded from this list --
# it keeps the external-reader exemption above. The one cited audit-trail
# counterexample (AM-cluster late-wake root cause, reference_am_cluster_late_wake_
# root_cause_2026-08-13.md) was reconstructed entirely from Windows Event Log +
# Claude Desktop's own logs, never from git history of these files -- so tracking
# them was not actually earning the audit-trail benefit it was kept for.
maintenance/_state/fleet-roster.md
maintenance/_state/model-canary.json
maintenance/_state/model-currency-cc.md
maintenance/_state/registry-membership.json
maintenance/_state/task-content-ledger.json
maintenance/_state/task-content-ledger.json.lock
maintenance/_state/wake-cause.json
# (2026-08-24, close-out work-order item 3) Six more maintenance/_state/ files audited
# individually against readers (grepped, not assumed) rather than swept as a class --
# fleet-heartbeat.json/health-guard-beacon.json/retire-pending.json are durable registers
# with an external or cross-session reader and stay TRACKED (see their own notes above /
# in pause-resume-guard.py); these three are pure local-probe run state, same class as
# phantom-dispatch.json above: dispatch-skip.json is dispatch-skip-probe.py's per-run
# snapshot (regenerated every automation-health-monitor invocation, read only within that
# same run); pause-resume-guard-state.json is load_state()/save_state()'s own private
# checkpoint, read/written only by pause-resume-guard.py itself; task-progress/ is
# task-progress-marker.py's per-task progress-marker directory, read only by that script
# and pause-resume-guard.py's stall check, no external consumer found.
maintenance/_state/dispatch-skip.json
maintenance/_state/pause-resume-guard-state.json
maintenance/_state/task-progress/
# (2026-08-26) log-liveness.json — _shared/log_liveness.py's per-run snapshot,
# written by ora-health-guard A.0d and re-read only within the same run. Same
# class as dispatch-skip.json / phantom-dispatch.json above: pure local-probe run
# state, regenerated every fire, no external or cross-session reader (grepped
# against fleet-deadman.yml, oxford-command-center and ora-pm, not assumed). The
# cross-fleet consumer reads the Connector Pre-Flight beacon's log_liveness line,
# not this file.
maintenance/_state/log-liveness.json
# (2026-09-10) ground-truth/last-auditor-run.json -- ground-truth-run-index.py's
# own "when did I last finish" marker (Sec 5 Stage 0's window-sizing input), read
# and written only by that script itself. Same class as pause-resume-guard-state.json
# above: no external or cross-session reader (the run-index document it feeds into
# is a separate, per-date file already handled by the script's own --out default,
# not this marker). Confirmed empty/absent before ora-ground-truth-auditor's first
# real run; a stray copy appears in any worktree that ran the CLI for testing.
maintenance/_state/ground-truth/last-auditor-run.json
# (2026-09-11, final-branch-review finding I7) ground-truth/run-index-*.json --
# per-night Stage 0 output, read only by the same night's SKILL.md run and by a
# human investigating that night. No external/cross-session reader.
maintenance/_state/ground-truth/run-index-*.json
# ground-truth-pending-approval/ -- drafted-but-never-sent corrections (Hard
# Invariant 1). Can reference confidential-deal-adjacent content if a run's
# claim touched one; must never be one `git add -A` away from landing in a
# git-tracked, off-machine-pushed repo. Never tracked.
maintenance/_state/ground-truth-pending-approval/
